XB-Kidux-Name-en: Photography
XB-Kidux-Description-en: A guide to taking photographs with a real camera: light, the shutter, the aperture, focus, composition, and drawing with light, with something to try in every chapter.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: Fotografía
XB-Kidux-Description-es: Una guía para hacer fotos con una cámara de verdad: la luz, el obturador, el diafragma, el enfoque, la composición y dibujar con luz, con algo que probar en cada capítulo.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 8-12
Description: Kidux learning module: Photography, a guide for a child with a real camera
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module is a guide for a child who has a camera in their hands: how the
 box with a hole that every camera is makes a picture, the shutter, the
 aperture and ISO, focus and depth of field, composition, and working with
 light, drawing with a torch in the dark included, one idea a chapter,
 with something to try with the camera in each, photographs that show
 each effect, and drawings of what the camera's screen shows. It names
 the Olympus XZ-2 as its example and says how to find the same controls
 on any other camera. Nothing of it comes from the internet.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
